    "body": "An admitted source view currently makes one query-based decision. This change lets a first read select an actual source occurrence, pass its retained K2 geometric value through a packed q4 finite H4 action, and read the same immutable keys again before the final joint Copy/Period/Stop decision.\n\nBoth atoms retain orientation, radius and presence status; their decoded sum is never projected into a root. Identity code1 wins ties. All final controllers use one updated snapshot, explicitly separated from original token replay. A matched RoleSurface input control uses identical producer/bridge shapes. Preparation removes the duplicate Period replay and checks frame/component/snapshot binding.\n\nExecuted source eada026ea1033f9bd713d02a830a4182d409ad69 passes88 focused Rust tests and release construction on Linux CPU. Restricted native-only execution independently preserves64parent own-prefix replies/all530action objects per baseline/identity,352available fullcontext positions, and530full identity-stage traces.178full contexts were not retained by the original run and are not reconstructed. Both unlearned nonzero modes change the refined snapshot and all three final score families64/64; produced value/action/snapshot differ on all64paired source/surface rows.\n\nBoth attempts320files67,045,658B return with exact SHA/file-set equality. The initial empty test filter is excluded and corrected; the first restricted replay fails before inference due to lost ELF-loader permissions and an overlapping owned-storage stop. Fresh repaired v2 passes, with all failures retained. Complete180min charge includes preparation/review/delivery; no optimizer/GPU/runners/new paid provisioning.\n\nExpanded finite/value tables remain dense prototype costs. Loading, tokenization and traces allocate. No learned benefit, default adoption, shared session edit, general attention/chat, complete-binary opcode, M1 performance or energy qualification is claimed. The next task is bridge-only ordinary final-token learning with frozen stage1/source keys/value producer, matched RoleSurface, native baseline-inclusive selection and new frozen transfer.\n\nReferences #1552\n",
